<newsitem itemid="226004" id="root" date="1996-11-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Northern Electric H1 pretax off, div 12.85p.</title>
<headline>Northern Electric H1 pretax off, div 12.85p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		31.2		   vs 45.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 12.85		  vs 12.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     50.7		   vs 58.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   440		    vs 429.8</p>
<p>NOTE - British regional electricity company Northern Electric Plc, fighting off a hostile bid from U.S. group CalEnergy Co Inc included a number of full-year forecasts with its interim results.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 55.5		   vs 56.9</p>
<p> Investment income	3.4		    vs 8.9</p>
<p> Net exceptional income 1.8		    vs 2.6 charge</p>
<p> Interest paid	    10.0		   vs 4.5</p>
<p> Tax			  13.2		   vs 16.0</p>
<p> Attributable	     37.5		   vs 7.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  n/a</p>
<p> Ex-div date		n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Northern Electric said it had resolved to pay the interim dividend in February 1997 &quot;if the offers by CE have previously lapsed, or otherwise as soon as possible&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
